    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hamill Estate Agents proudly present No.63 Ennafort Road, Raheny, Dublin 5 to the Sales Market — a well-maintained three-bedroom semi-detached family home, tucked away in a quiet and mature cul-de-sac in this most sought-after residential area.\r\n\r\nMeasuring approximately 110 sq. m, the property is presented in good condition throughout, while offering an exciting opportunity for the new owners to modernise and upgrade to their own taste and style.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are greeted by a welcoming entrance hall, leading to a good-sized family room, double doors into the living room with fireplace, overlooking the extensive rear garden. The kitchen is located off the hallway and interconnects with the dining area, which could equally service as an additional sitting room or playroom. A large bathroom/shower room is conveniently located just off this room. \r\n\r\nAn attribute to this property is the sunroom, which is accessed from the dining room and kitchen, creating a bright and versatile additional living space.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises two well-proportioned double bedrooms, a smaller bedroom and a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nExternally, the home boasts a generous gated front garden with ample off-street parking and direct access to the useful garage. The rear garden is probably the outstanding feature of this property. Extending to approximately 90 foot in length, this space is magnificent, not overlooked and consists of a sizeable lawn with boundary walls/fencing and mature planting. This very private outdoor space is ideal for outdoor dining and relaxation.\r\n\r\nEnnafort Road is a much sought-after address in Raheny, renowned for its peaceful surroundings and close-knit community. The property enjoys easy access to Raheny Village, which offers a superb range of shops, cafés, and restaurants, as well as Raheny DART Station, excellent bus services, and the M1 and M50 motorways. The area is also close to several well-regarded schools, St. Anne’s Park, and the Seafront at Bull Island.\r\n\r\nNo. 63 Ennafort Road represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a solid family home in a prime location, with substantial gardens and offers potential to modernise and create a dream home in the heart of Raheny.\r\n\r\nViewing comes highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall: 3.92m x 1.71m\t\t\tTimber floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 4.28m x 3.40m\t\tCarpet flooring, and a fireplace.\r\n\r\nFamily Room: 3.91m x 2.68m\t        Laminate flooring, and double doors to the living room.\r\n\r\nDining Room: .78m x 2.62m\t\tOpen to the kitchen.\r\n\r\nSun Room: 3.10m x 2.86m\t\tWith a laminate floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen: 3.19m x 2.22m \t\t        With wall and floor units, and a tiled splashback.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\nBedroom 1: 4.24m x 3.42m \t   \tDouble bedroom with carpet flooring and built in wardrobes. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 3.94m x 2.84m \t   \tCarpet flooring and a built in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 3.28m x 2.25m \t   \tCarpet flooring. \r\n\r\nBathroom: 1.87m x 1.67m\t        With a shower, w.h.b. & w.c. \r\n\r\nShower Room: 2.76m x 2.72m\tFully tiled and with a shower, w.h.b. & w.c. \r\n\r\nGarage: 2.84m x 2.08m\t\t\tFully tiled and with a bath, w.h.b. & w.c."
